clarify::clear-06.text:
The distance was \(4.8\) km and the time was \(\frac{40}{60}= \frac{2}{3}\) hour.

\[
\text{speed} = \frac{\text{distance}}{\text{time}} 
               = \frac{4.8}{\,\frac{2}{3}\,}
               = 4.8 \times \frac{3}{2}
               = 7.2\ \text{km/h}.
\]

So the cyclist’s average speed is **\(7.2\) kilometers per hour**.

